The sampler stream never loses samples silently.

The RT sampler does not wait for its readers: one that falls more than the
ring's depth behind loses the oldest samples.  That cannot be prevented, only
made visible, so every segment on the wire carries the index of its first
sample, and halsampler reports each gap on stderr, numbers its -t output across
the gap, and exits 1.

Two samplers record their own sample numbers, so every output line can be
checked against its number.  "lossy" (ring of two, 100 us thread) loses samples
on every poll; the test checks that the numbers skip exactly what stderr
reports.  "roomy" (ring of ten seconds) must lose nothing.
